<.masthead payload={@payload} slug={@slug} current={:register} />

<section>
  <h2>Entry sent</h2>

  <p>
    The details for <strong>{@name}</strong>
    are in the queue for the arbiter of {Tournament.name(@payload)}.
  </p>

  <p class="footnote">
    <strong>This is not a place in the tournament.</strong>
    The arbiter reads this queue on their own machine and decides who plays.
    You will not appear on the <a href={~p"/t/#{@slug}"}>standings</a>, in a
    pairing, or anywhere else on this site until they have entered you and
    published a round - and if they need to ask you something first, they will
    use the address you gave.
  </p>

  <p class="footnote">
    Sent it twice, or spotted a mistake? Send it again and say so in the name
    field, or write to the organisers. Nothing on this page can edit or delete
    an entry: sorting out two entries for the same player is the arbiter's job,
    the same as it is with a paper form.
  </p>

  <p><a href={~p"/t/#{@slug}"}>Back to {Tournament.name(@payload)}</a></p>
</section>
